WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.136
-My first guest is
an Oscar winner starring

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.937
alongside Denzel Washington
and Rami Malek

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:07.073
in the new thriller
"The Little Things,"

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.175
which will be in theaters
Friday, January 29th,

00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:12.211
and available on HBO Max.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.647
Here is my man Jared Leto!

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.749
That's what
I'm talkin' about. Yes!

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.384
Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.820
The applause is deafening.
-Thank you.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.155
They multiply it
when we air the show.

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.792
It sounds like
there's five people doing this.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.361
-Oh, five people? Oh, nice.
That feels so good.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.762
Just feels so good to be home.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.165
-[ Laughs ]
Can you believe this?

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.434
The last time I saw you
was at the Met Gala.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.605
The big Met Gala in 2019.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.207
-That was the last time
we saw each other.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.875
And it was --
I couldn't believe --

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.178
I thought I've seen you
since then, but I guess not.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:49.148
But it was very memorable
for me because, you know,

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.317
these Met Galas are giant
and everyone gets dressed up.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.653
And all the money
goes to a good cause, you know,

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.255
and all that stuff,
for the Met Museum --

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:59.492
Metropolitan Museum of Art.
But everyone's dressed up.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.429
I think the theme of the night
was camp,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:06.232
and you carried around
your own head.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.100
Uh, we have a couple of photos.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.069
Can we take a look back
a couple years ago?

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:13.606
Look. This is unbelievable.
It was -- [ Laughs ]

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:18.043
It was -- Yo. My G--

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.746
What --
What was the inspiration?

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.814
Do you remember coming out
and going like,

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.148
"Yeah, I'm gonna do this"?

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:25.184
-I think there might be
picture of you and I,

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.153
or maybe you with my head --
I'm not sure --

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.587
somewhere from that night.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:32.192
-Do we have one? Oh, yeah.
That's me, you, and your head.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.126
-♪ Just the three of us ♪

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:36.996
-Oh, yeah. Then I pulled that
move, which was even weirder.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.832
I've kind of put your head
where my head is.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:43.168
-[ Laughter ]
-It was so fun that night.

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:45.271
Everyone was holding --
-Yeah, it was a blast.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:48.508
I remember I walked
out of the hotel,

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.275
and there were
all throngs of people,

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:53.712
like, kind of greeting folks
as they left the hotel.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.948
And I walked through the hotel,
and for some reason,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:59.519
just held the head up to the
crowd, and they just roared.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.488
And I thought,
"This is so strange."

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.857
I don't know what, you know --
I don't know what it was,

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.992
but it was just a weird --
It was a very weird thing,

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:08.494
but a very fun thing, too.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:11.430
-You know, I thought about you.
I wanted to reach out to you.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.633
But I figured everyone was
probably reaching out to you.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.303
When the quarantine
first began --

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.505
and you probably know
what I'm about to say --

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:24.410
I couldn't imagine this
happening to me or to anyone.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.580
But you didn't even know that
everything had been shut down.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.415
You were on a retreat.
Is this true?

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.917
-Absolutely true, yeah.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.919
It's like a two-week, roughly
two-week silent meditation.

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.723
The idea is that you go away.
You get rid of your phone.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.257
You get rid of distractions.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:41.794
You get rid of everything.
And you just meditate.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:46.799
And when I went away,
there were about 150 cases.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:51.004
Uh, and just in that
short amount of time,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.472
when I came out,
it was shut down,

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:56.475
a state of emergency, uh,
and the whole world had changed.

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:58.378
But when we're in there,
they didn't tell us.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:01.514
So we didn't have our phones.
There was no talking, of course.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:05.051
-No TV.
-No eye contact. No TV.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.986
Um, and the teachers
didn't really --

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.456
They made a decision. "Let's not
disturb the participants."

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.792
-Oh, my goodness.
-And I didn't turn on my phone

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.493
until I went back to LA.

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.662
So, I drove the whole way,

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:19.432
you know, trying to be,
like, peaceful and zen.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.999
Keep the feeling going.

00:03:20.999 --> 00:03:24.470
And I got back, and I was,
you know, kind of shocked.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.138
It was like Rip Van Winkle.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:28.174
-I mean, it's like
a "Twilight Zone" episode,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.777
but in real life.
-Yeah, it was shocking.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.112
It was a great --
I had this great tool

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.048
to kind of deal with "stress"
and things in life,

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:39.819
but I don't think anything
can quite prepare any of us

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.222
for what we all went through
at the beginning.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.391
-No. Oh, my goodness. No way.
But I thought of you.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.993
I go, "Oh, my goodness. I can't
wait to talk to you about that."

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:50.262
Because that sounds like
the most bizarre story.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.898
-Yeah, it was like coming out
to the zombie apocalypse.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.934
-Yeah, I got to say
you knocked it out of the park

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.069
for "The Little Things,"

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:01.340
which is coming out this Friday
in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.644
You did it great.
This is so good.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.012
Dude, you're so --

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.580
The whole movie,
I'm just going like,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.183
"Oh, no. Whoa.
This guy's so creepy, man."

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:14.187
It didn't even look like you.
Was that -- You had a fake nose?

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.856
-I had a lot of stuff going on.
Yeah, it was --

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.558
First of all,
I had an opportunity to work

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.728
with Denzel Washington,
one of my heroes.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.730
For me, he's like
Brando and Beethoven.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.766
-What was that like?

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.802
-He's just --
He's just, you know --

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.905
He's the GOAT. He's the king.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.007
And, yeah, it was
a whole transformation.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:38.577
I had different -- had
brown eyes, a different nose,

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:41.380
different teeth, a different way
of walking and talking,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:46.752
and it was just this
super-immersive character.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:49.088
-How do we describe the movie
and who you play in the movie?

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.090
It's great.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.227
-Well, the name says a lot. I
play a guy named Albert Sparma.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.662
And right from the name,
you can tell

00:04:56.662 --> 00:05:00.700
he's a little different
and a bit of an outsider.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.635
But I found him
to be really funny.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:06.472
He had a pretty crazy
sense of humor.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:09.108
It was a special one. Something
really special about this.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.544
With Rami Malek and Denzel --
just to get in the ring

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.914
with those two guys was --
I felt really, really fortunate.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.582
-I want to show a clip.
Here is Jared Leto

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.151
and Denzel Washington
in "The Little Things."

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.887
Take a look at this.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.721
-I saw the "for sale" sign.

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:25.123
-That was for another car.

00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:28.126
-Got a lot of miles on it.
You a -- You a salesman?

00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:31.197
-[ Scoffs ] No.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.899
-How's the trunk space?

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:40.573
-Standard.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.075
-Mind if I take a look?

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:46.245
I'm in the market.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.679
-It's not for sale.

00:05:47.679 --> 00:05:51.183
-All I need to do
is take a look.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:54.020
-You must really like my car.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.189
-I do.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.229
-Jared Leto, everybody.

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.765
"The Little Things" will be
in theaters this Friday

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:08.368
and available on HBO Max.

